# test/planar_embankment/test_planar_embankment.jl
# =====================================================
# Planar slope + thin embankment SGS validation test
#
# Terrain (generated by generate_planar_embankment_dem.py):
#   - Linear planar slope west→east (default 0.1%, total relief 4 m).
#   - Thin rectangular embankment at x=50% of domain (default 2 m high, 20 m wide).
#   - A 3 m notch (gap) centred at y=0.5*Ly — narrower than a res-18 A5
#     cell (~22 m diameter), so sub-cell for the standard solver.
#   - Injection point at x=0.1*Lx, y=0.5*Ly (well upstream of embankment).
#
# Key design intent:
#   The planar slope gives perfectly predictable flow: water injected upstream
#   flows east until it meets the embankment and ponds.  Standard flow sees
#   only cell-mean elevations, so it cannot detect the 3 m notch and must
#   wait until upstream WSE exceeds the embankment crest (emb_crest_z) before
#   routing water downstream.  SGS pre-computes the minimum DEM elevation along
#   each shared cell boundary, so it detects the notch and routes water at the
#   notch sill elevation (= local slope elevation at the embankment, ~2 m below
#   crest) — well before the standard solver acts.
#
# Test assertions:
#   T0 — Mesh sanity: cells exist on both sides of the embankment for both meshes.
#   T1 — Standard flow: no downstream water until upstream WSE ≥ emb_crest_z.
#   T2 — SGS: downstream water appears well before upstream WSE ≥ emb_crest_z.
#   T3 — At the same injection history, SGS routes more water downstream than
#        standard (and does so at lower upstream head).
#   T4 — Mass balance < 0.01% for both solvers (closed boundaries, no outflow).
#   T5 — HDF5 output files are valid: correct frame count, non-zero depth values.
#
# Usage:
#   # Step 1 — generate DEM (once, or if defaults changed):
#   python test/planar_embankment/generate_planar_embankment_dem.py
#
#   # Step 2 — delete old meshes if DEM changed:
#   Remove-Item test/planar_embankment/planar_mesh18_sgs.parquet -ErrorAction Ignore
#   Remove-Item test/planar_embankment/planar_mesh18_std.parquet -ErrorAction Ignore
#
#   # Step 3 — run tests (meshes are auto-generated if absent):
#   julia --threads auto test/planar_embankment/test_planar_embankment.jl
#
#   # Optional: run with Makie visualisation (standard flow):
#   julia --threads auto test/planar_embankment/test_planar_embankment.jl --vis

